    {
      "url": "https://www.senate.mn/schedule/hearing_minutes.html?always_show_minutes=Y&hearing_id=17687&ls=93&type=minutes",
      "sha256": "187af02d788e0787d57ee96e00b0ed6ae4d8acbdd94f9aeaee3bb78c09a7ff66",
      "textSha256": "187af02d788e0787d57ee96e00b0ed6ae4d8acbdd94f9aeaee3bb78c09a7ff66",
      "format": "html",
      "date": "2023-03-07",
      "committee": "Elections",
      "session_slug": "2023-2024",
      "text": "Present : Senator Jim Carlson - Chair, Senator Bonnie S. Westlin Vice Chair, Senator Bruce D. Anderson, Senator Calvin K. Bahr, Senator Liz Boldon, Senator Steve A. Cwodzinski, Senator Gene Dornink, Senator Mark W. Koran, Senator Warren Limmer, Senator John Marty, Senator Andrew Mathews, Senator Nicole Mitchell, Senator Lindsey Port, Senator Ann H. Rest\n Absent : No Members Absent\n Senator Jim Carlson called the meeting to order at 3:08 PM.\n Call to order \n S.F. 1548: Senator Rest: A delete everything amendment will replace the current language with ongoing \nfunding for local governments for expenses directly related to administering \nelections. \n Testifiers: \n Senator Rest\n Michelle Clasen, Washington County Commissioner, Association of Minnesota Counties\n Michael Stalberger, Property and Environmental Resources Director, Blue Earth County\n (zoom) Cathy Sorensen, City Clerk, City of Blaine\n Minnesota Secretary of State Steve Simon\n Senator Rest moved the A2 Author's Amendment. By a voice vote, the motion prevailed, and the A2 Author's Amendment was adopted.\n Senator Rest moved the A3 Amendment. By a voice vote, the motion prevailed, and that A3 Amendment was adopted.\n Senator Rest moved that SF 1548, as amended, be recommended to pass, and re-referred to the Taxes Committee. By a voice vote, the motion prevailed.\nSenator Rest moved that S.F. 1548, as amended, recommended to pass and re-referred to the Taxes Committee. - MOTION PREVAILED .\n S.F. 2051: Senator Boldon: Lobbying provisions expansion to include all political subdivisions. \n Testifiers: \n Senator Boldon\n Jeff Sigurdson, Executive Director, Minnesota Campaign Finance Board\n Senator Boldon moved the A1 Author's Amendment. By a voice vote, the motion prevailed, and the A1 Author's Amendment was adopted.\n Senator Koran moved the A2 Amendment and requested a roll call and a roll call was granted.\n Senator Carlson - nay\n Senator Westlin - nay\n Senator Koran - yay\n Senator Anderson - yay\n Senator Bahr - pass\n Senator Boldon - nay\n Senator Cwodzinski - nay\n Senator Dornink - yay\n Senator Limmer - yay\n Senator Marty - nay\n Senator Mathews - yay\n Senator Mitchell - nay\n Senator Port - nay\n Senator Rest - nay\n By a roll call vote of 5 yays, 8 nays, and 1 pass, the motion failed, and the A2 Amendment was not adopted.\n Senator Carlson moved that SF 2051, as amended, be laid over. By a voice vote, the motion prevailed.\nSenator Carlson moved that S.F. 2051, as amended, laid over for possible inclusion in the omnibus bill. - MOTION PREVAILED .\n The meeting was adjourned at 4:30 PM.\nSenator Jim Carlson, Chair\nTaylor Spreeman, Legislative Assistant"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.lrl.mn.gov/archive/minutes/senate/2023/elections/20230403/Elections_20230403_Minutes.pdf",
      "sha256": "fb4076f1ffdd09494eb86d2eebf646043cc4173ccfad6ec87fc57bdbbf4f35cb",
      "textSha256": "159fd1de51000e6679f51596557d01be94764397651df2bf61441aa9c4e3bb34",
      "format": "pdf",
      "date": "2023-04-03",
      "committee": "Elections",
      "session_slug": "2023-2024",
      "text": "Elections Committee\nMonday, April 3, 2023\n12:30 PM, Room 1200, Minnesota Senate Bldg.\nMinutes\nPresent: Senator Jim Carlson - Chair, Senator Bonnie S. Westlin Vice Chair, Senator Bruce D. Anderson,\nSenator Calvin K. Bahr, Senator Liz Boldon, Senator Steve A. Cwodzinski, Senator Gene Dornink,\nSenator Mark W. Koran, Senator Warren Limmer, Senator John Marty, Senator Andrew Mathews,\nSenator Nicole L. Mitchell, Senator Lindsey Port, Senator Ann H. Rest\nAbsent: No Members Absent\nSenator Bonnie S. Westlin called the meeting to order at 12:44 PM.\nCall to order\nS.F. 1636: Senator Carlson: Elections Budget Omnibus Bill.\nTestifiers:\nSenator Carlson\nAndrew Erickson, Elections Committee Fiscal Analyst\nAlexis Stangl, Elections Committee Counsel\nNicole Freeman, Government Relations Director, Office of the Secretary of State\nMary Hartnett, Executive Director, Clean Elections Minnesota\nRick Heller, Citizen\nSenator Carlson moved the A24 Amendment and asked to incorporate A27 Amendment into A24\nAmendment. By a voice vote, the motion prevailed, and the A24 Amendment with the A27 Amendment\nincorporated into it was adopted.\nSenator Koran moved the A25 Amendment and requested a roll call, and a roll call was granted.\nSenator Carlson – nay\nSenator Westlin – nay\nSenator Koran – yay\nSenator Anderson – yay\nSenator Bahr – yay\nSenator Boldon – nay\nSenator Cwodzinski – nay\nSenator Dornink – yay\nSenator Limmer – yay\nSenator Marty – nay\nSenator Mathews – yay\nSenator Mitchell – nay\nSenator Port – nay\nSenator Rest - nay\nBy a roll call vote of 6 yays and 8 nays, the motion failed, and the A25 Amendment was not adopted.\nSenator Koran moved the A28 Amendment and requested a roll call, and a roll call was granted.\nSenator Carlson – nay\nSenator Westlin – nay\nSenator Koran – yay\nSenator Anderson – yay\n\n-- 1 of 2 --\n\nSenator Bahr – yay\nSenator Boldon – nay\nSenator Cwodzinski – nay\nSenator Dornink – yay\nSenator Limmer – yay\nSenator Marty – nay\nSenator Mathews – yay\nSenator Mitchell – nay\nSenator Port – nay\nSenator Rest - nay\nBy a roll call vote of 6 yays and 8 nays, the motion failed, and the A28 Amendment was not adopted.\nSenator Westlin moved that SF 1636, as amended, be recommended to pass and re-referred to the\nCommittee on Finance. Senator Koran requested a roll call and a roll call was granted.\nSenator Carlson – yay\nSenator Westlin – yay\nSenator Koran – nay\nSenator Anderson – nay\nSenator Bahr – nay\nSenator Boldon – yay\nSenator Cwodzinski – yay\nSenator Dornink – nay\nSenator Limmer – nay\nSenator Marty – yay\nSenator Mathews – nay\nSenator Mitchell – yay\nSenator Port – yay\nSenator Rest - yay\nBy a roll call vote of 8 yays and 6 nays, the motion prevailed.\nSenator Westlin moved that S.F. 1636, as amended, recommended to pass and re-referred to the\nFinance Committee. - MOTION PREVAILED.\nThe meeting was adjourned at 1:27 PM.\nSenator Jim Carlson, Chair\nChristie Blood, Legislative Assistant for\nTaylor Spreeman, Legislative Assistant\n\n-- 2 of 2 --"
    }
